  "body": "Found while reviewing #715 (grblHAL post).\n\nWhat happens: #635 (#616) added an opt-in \"Smoothing per operation\" post option that every mill dialect writes as its control's word (G64 P, G5.1, G187, CYCLE832, G62). Fanuc and Mazak write a one-time \"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN\" note when they can't state a word. `assets/posts/carvera.cps` never reads `Smoothing` / `SmoothingMode`, so a Carvera document with smoothing switched on posts no smoothing word and no note. The user believes smoothing is on, and the program says nothing.\n\nExpected: the Carvera post either writes the word its controller supports, or writes the same one-time \"not written\" note as Fanuc and Mazak. A case in `crates/app/tests/smoothing.rs` pins it.\n\nEffort: high because of the safety floor (it changes posted G-code), though the change is small.\n\nDone means: Carvera with smoothing on posts a smoothing word or the one-time note, pinned by a `smoothing.rs` case and a golden.\n",
